<article class="env-definition" id="04F4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04F4">Definition <span data-tag="04F4">37.7.2</span>.</a> Let $h : Z \to X$ be a formally unramified morphism of schemes. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The <em>universal first order thickening</em> of $Z$ over $X$ is the thickening $Z \subset Z'$ constructed in Lemma <a href="/tag/04F3" data-tag="04F3">37.7.1</a>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The <em>conormal sheaf of $Z$ over $X$</em> is the conormal sheaf of $Z$ in its universal first order thickening $Z'$ over $X$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> We often denote the conormal sheaf $\mathcal{C}_{Z/X}$ in this situation. </p>
</article>